.DS_Store
/.build
# All *.nosync scratch (SwiftPM/DerivedData/venv plus per-agent build dirs) —
# iCloud-excluded build state, never committed. The anchored entries below are
# kept for history; the pattern covers them and any future .nosync dir.
*.nosync
/.build.nosync
/.deriveddata.nosync
/.venv.nosync
/.swiftpm
/runs/
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
.netrc
*.profraw

# Server durable job store (SQLite) — runtime state, never committed.
.steerlab/

# One-click local-server pidfile (scripts/start-local-server.sh) — runtime
# adoption record at the workspace root, never committed.
.steerlab-local-server.pid

# Researcher-specific study data (case families, items, human-baseline
# worksheets, scoring notes). This repo's prompts/ is seed/template data and
# test fixtures only — study data belongs in a WORKSPACE, where freeze can
# pin and auto-commit it. Third-party paper full-texts are also never
# committed (copyright + history bloat); keep local-only names in
# .git/info/exclude.
/prompts/studies/
# Deploy-written build identity (rsync deploys carry no .git; see build_identity.py)
Server/steerlab_server/BUILD_COMMIT
# Home-layout workspaces (decision 8): SteerLab's home folder holds
# Workspaces/ BESIDE the checkout, so these never appear inside the repo —
# this ignore is the belt-and-suspenders for a hand-created nested one, and
# the public scanner tier refuses any tracked path beneath them.
Workspaces/
workspaces/
